# Workflow expressions

Open Workflow task values can contain expressions evaluated by the shared
`open-agent-core` runtime. Use `${ ... }` for a complete value or interpolation;
paths beginning with `.` or `$` may also be used directly. A plain path such as
`context.name` is evaluated when it appears inside `${ ... }`.

## Paths and prefixes

| Prefix | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `input.` or `$workflow.input.` | The workflow invocation payload |
| `context.` or `values.` | The mutable execution state |
| `.` or `$` | Shorthand for the invocation payload |

Missing paths evaluate to `None` rather than raising.

## Literals and operators

Expressions support literals (quoted strings, numbers, booleans, null, JSON
lists, and JSON objects),
unary `!`, binary `||`/`or`, `&&`/`and`, comparisons, and membership tests
(`in` / `not in`).

## Built-in functions

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `length(value)` | Length of a string, list, or dict; `0` for `None` |
| `upper(value)` | Upper-case string conversion |
| `lower(value)` | Lower-case string conversion |
| `concat(a, b, ...)` | Concatenate arguments as strings |
| `join(separator, items)` | Join a list with a separator |
| `split(value, separator)` | Split a string into a list |
| `default(value, fallback)` | Return `fallback` when `value` is `None` |
| `exists(value)` | `True` when `value` is not `None` |
| `matches(value, pattern)` | `True` when `value` matches a Python regex |
| `now()` | Current UTC ISO-8601 timestamp |

Functions may be nested, for example `length(split(context.tags, ','))`.

## Coercion and error matrix

| Operation | Non-string operand | `None` operand | Out-of-range index |
|-----------|-------------------|----------------|-------------------|
| `length` | Uses Python `len`; `0` if unsupported | `0` | N/A |
| `upper`/`lower` | Coerced with `str` | `"NONE"` / `"none"` | N/A |
| `concat`/`join` | Coerced with `str` | Coerced to `"None"` | N/A |
| `split` | Coerced with `str` | Coerced to `"None"` | N/A |
| `matches` | Coerced with `str` | Coerced to `"None"` | N/A |
| Ordered comparison | Type mismatch returns `False` | Type mismatch returns `False` | N/A |
| Path lookup | `None` | `None` | `None` |

Unknown functions raise a runtime `RuntimeError`.

## Scoped variables in loops

`for` tasks bind an `each` variable and an optional `at` index. Nested loops
that reuse the same variable name shadow the outer binding only for the
inner loop body; the outer value is restored after the inner loop completes.
